    15	## Panel golden gate
    16	
    17	The central comparison policy is reasonable for finite data:
    18	
    19	- The frozen reconstruction sequence matches the production builder at [panel_golden_gate.py:58](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/scripts/generalization/panel_golden_gate.py:58).
    20	- Exact canonical-CSV equality for non-BJD science columns is appropriate at [panel_golden_gate.py:71](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/scripts/generalization/panel_golden_gate.py:71).
    21	- A one-ULP BJD tolerance and one-ULP carried-metadata tolerance are scientifically negligible and consistent with the documented reserialization issue.
    22	
    23	The implementation is not yet fail-closed:
    24	
    25	1. **NaNs pass as `identical_1ulp`.** The ULP expressions at [panel_golden_gate.py:81](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/scripts/generalization/panel_golden_gate.py:81) and [panel_golden_gate.py:95](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/scripts/generalization/panel_golden_gate.py:95) produce NaN; comparisons such as `NaN > 1` are false. A focused check confirmed that replacing either BJD or RA with NaN was accepted. Require matching finite masks and finite values before ULP comparison.
    26	
    27	2. **Vacuous pass is possible.** `--count` is not validated at [panel_golden_gate.py:123](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/scripts/generalization/panel_golden_gate.py:123), and `all([])` passes at [panel_golden_gate.py:147](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/scripts/generalization/panel_golden_gate.py:147). Require `count >= 1`, nonempty records, unique IDs, and the expected sample count/digest.
    28	
    29	3. **It is not operationally a gate.** Its report lacks frozen, campaign, roster, exposure, and raw-cache hashes, and neither the panel builder nor runner requires a matching panel attestation. The existing five-star PASS therefore remains an unbound smoke test.
    30	
    31	Minor documentation cleanup: [metrics_generalization.py:11](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/scripts/generalization/metrics_generalization.py:11) still says D2 truth uses `d2_modes.csv`, contradicting its corrected implementation.
